```java
package com.acme.billing;

public final class InvoiceDtos {

    private InvoiceDtos() {}

    public record InvoiceResponse(
            long id,
            long customerId,
            long amountCents,
            String status,
            String issuedAt) {

        public static InvoiceResponse from(Invoice invoice) {
            return new InvoiceResponse(
                    invoice.getId(),
                    invoice.getCustomerId(),
                    invoice.getAmountCents(),
                    invoice.getStatus().name(),
                    invoice.getIssuedAt().toString());
        }
    }
}
```

Notes:
- Constructor injection for `InvoiceService`, no Lombok/`@Autowired`; response wrapped in `ApiResponse.ok(...)`, no raw entity returned.
- No try/catch in the controller — if `getInvoice` throws a not-found domain exception, it's expected to be mapped by an existing `@RestControllerAdvice`. Adjust `Invoice` field names/`ApiResponse` package to match your actual types.

